Package: castSDM
Type: Package
Title: Causal Variable Selection for Species Distribution Modeling
Version: 0.6.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
            "Liqiang", "Q",
      email = "2759831686@qq.com",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-6966-4633")
    )
  )
Description: Provides an end-to-end species distribution modeling workflow
    built around a causal variable-selection engine. By default the conditional
    predictive impact (Watson & Wright 2021) tests each predictor's conditional
    independence from occurrence given the others with a cross-fitted random
    forest and knockoffs, so nonlinear (including symmetric unimodal) niche
    responses are detected; an optional double machine learning selector
    (Chernozhukov et al. 2018) estimates signed orthogonalized partial-linear
    effects. Predictors surviving Benjamini-Hochberg FDR control are retained.
    The package couples this screen with standard SDM algorithms (Random
    Forest, BRT, MaxEnt, GAM), nested spatial cross-validation, ensemble
    prediction, future climate projection with extrapolation control, and a
    counterfactual what-if interpretation layer. It supports transferable
    prediction and interpretable driver analysis but does not claim automatic
    discovery of ecological causes.
